module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.Cosimplicial.CompletedDifferentials

/-!
# The completed differential forms of the cosimplicial envelope are homotopic to zero

Work in an affine crystalline situation `(A, I, γ)` with target `C`, choose a polynomial algebra
`P = A[x_i]` over `A` and a surjection `P → C`, and let `D(*)` be the cosimplicial ring of
`p`-adically completed divided power envelopes of the kernels `J(n)` of the surjections onto `C`
from the `(n + 1)`-fold tensor powers of `P`, with its cosimplicial module `Ω_{D(*)}` of
`p`-adically completed divided power differentials.  Write `Ω^i_{D(n)}` for the `p`-adic
completion of the `i`-th exterior power of `Ω_{D(n)}`.

This file proves that for every cosimplicial module `M_*` over `D(*)` and every `i > 0` the
cosimplicial module

`M_0 ⊗̂_{D(0)} Ω^i_{D(0)} → M_1 ⊗̂_{D(1)} Ω^i_{D(1)} → M_2 ⊗̂_{D(2)} Ω^i_{D(2)} → ⋯`,

the `p`-adic completion of the degreewise tensor product of `M_*` with `Ω^i_{D(*)}`, is homotopic
to zero.  The argument of the source is followed step by step: the identity and the zero
endomorphism of `Ω_{D(*)}` are homotopic, an exterior power of a homotopy is a homotopy, a
positive exterior power of the zero map is zero, completion and tensoring preserve homotopies, so
each of the four operations applied to `Ω_{D(*)}` leaves the identity homotopic to zero.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.adicCompletionMapₛₗ` — the map of adic completions induced by a semilinear map
  which carries the one adic ideal into the other.
* `Crystalline.SemilinearCosimplicialModule.toCosimplicialModule` — a cosimplicial module given
  by its degreewise modules and semilinear transition maps, read as a presheaf of modules over
  the presheaf of rings of the cosimplicial ring.
* `Crystalline.CosimplicialIdeal.completion` — the degreewise adic completion of a cosimplicial
  module along a cosimplicial ideal, with `Crystalline.CosimplicialIdeal.completionHom` on
  homomorphisms and `Crystalline.CosimplicialIdeal.completionHomotopy` on homotopies.
* `Crystalline.pAdicCosimplicialIdeal` — the ideals `(p) ⊆ D(n)` as a cosimplicial ideal.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.id_completedTensorCompletedForms_homotopic_zero` — Tag 07LA: for `i > 0` the
  cosimplicial module `M_* ⊗̂_{D(*)} Ω^i_{D(*)}` is homotopic to zero.
* `Crystalline.homotopic_completionHom` and `Crystalline.homotopic_id_completion_zero` —
  degreewise adic completion preserves homotopies of homomorphisms of cosimplicial modules.
* `Crystalline.homotopic_id_tensor` — tensoring on the left preserves homotopies.
* `Crystalline.exteriorPowerFunctor_map_zero` and
  `Crystalline.homotopic_id_exteriorPower_zero` — a positive exterior power of the zero
  homomorphism is zero, so a positive exterior power of a cosimplicial module whose identity is
  homotopic to zero has the same property.  This is where the hypothesis `i > 0` of the tag is
  used: for `i = 0` the exterior power of the zero map is the identity.

## Implementation notes

"Homotopic to zero" is `Crystalline.Homotopic (𝟙 _) 0`, the notion of Tag 07KQ which Tag 07L9
already uses: the identity endomorphism of the cosimplicial module is related to its zero
endomorphism by the equivalence relation generated by the degreewise linear homotopies indexed by
the simplices of `Δ[1]`.  All four steps of the proof are stability properties of exactly that
relation, which is why the proof of the source goes through verbatim.

Tag 07KQ is formalized twice over, once for each of the two presentations of a cosimplicial
module: its tensor and exterior power parts for presheaves of modules, its completion part for
the hand-bundled `Crystalline.SemilinearCosimplicialModule`, whose carriers may live in a
universe independent of the universe of the rings.  The proof of this tag needs to complete,
then tensor, then complete again, so it needs the completion statement in the presheaf
presentation; `Crystalline.homotopic_completionHom` is that statement, proved here directly
rather than transported, and it carries no tag because the tag for the completion part of 07KQ
is already placed on `Crystalline.homotopic_adicCompletionMap`.  For the same reason
`Crystalline.homotopic_id_tensor`, the left-handed companion of the tagged right-handed
`Crystalline.homotopic_tensor_id`, is untagged.

The degreewise completion is *constructed*, not axiomatized by an interface: its degrees are
Mathlib's `AdicCompletion` of the degrees of the original module and its transition maps are the
canonical semilinear extensions `Crystalline.adicCompletionMapₛₗ` of the original ones.  The
construction is routed through `SemilinearCosimplicialModule.toCosimplicialModule`, whose
transition identities are degreewise equations of elements; a presheaf of modules asks instead
for its `map_id` to be the inverse of `ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'`, and checking that equation
directly against the adic completion of a degree of a presheaf of modules sends the definitional
unfolding of the submodules `(p)^n • ⊤` into a divergence.  Proving it once, where the degrees are
opaque types, avoids this.

The naturality of the completed homomorphisms and of the completed homotopies is the same
statement twice, so it is proved once as `Crystalline.completion_naturality`: both sides are
adically continuous and agree on the canonical image of the uncompleted module, which is dense.

As in Tag 07L9 the cosimplicial envelope is taken as a hypothesis, through the structure
`Crystalline.CosimplicialEnvelope` which pins down `D(*)` and `Ω_{D(*)}`; nothing here constructs
one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 60.21.2, Tag 07LA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07LA)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 60.21.1, Tag 07L9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07L9)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 60.16.1, Tag 07KQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07KQ)
* [Stacks Project, Equation 60.17.3, Tag 07JF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07JF)
* [Stacks Project, Equation 60.21.1, Tag 07L0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07L0)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory Opposite Simplicial

universe u v w

namespace Crystalline

/-! ### Semilinear maps of adic completions -/

section SemilinearCompletion

variable {R S : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] {P Q : Type*}
  [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P] [AddCommGroup Q] [Module S Q]
  {σ : R →+* S} {I : Ideal R} {J : Ideal S}

/-- A semilinear map which carries one ideal into the other carries the submodules cutting out
the adic filtration into one another. -/
public lemma pow_smul_top_le_comap (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (h : I.map σ ≤ J) (n : ℕ) :
    I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule R P) ≤ (J ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule S Q)).comap g := by
  apply Submodule.smul_le.mpr
  intro r hr x _
  change g (r • x) ∈ J ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule S Q)
  rw [g.map_smulₛₗ]
  refine Submodule.smul_mem_smul ?_ Submodule.mem_top
  have hr' : σ r ∈ (I.map σ) ^ n := by
    rw [← Ideal.map_pow]
    exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem σ hr
  exact (pow_le_pow_left' h n) hr'

/-- The map induced on the `n`-th stages of two adic completions by a semilinear map which
carries the one adic ideal into the other. -/
public noncomputable def adicQuotientMap (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (h : I.map σ ≤ J) (n : ℕ) :
    (P ⧸ I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule R P)) →ₛₗ[σ] (Q ⧸ J ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule S Q)) :=
  Submodule.mapQ _ _ g (pow_smul_top_le_comap g h n)

/-- `adicQuotientMap` acts on the class of an element `a` as the class of its image. -/
private lemma adicQuotientMap_mkQ (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (h : I.map σ ≤ J) (n : ℕ) (a : P) :
    adicQuotientMap g h n (Submodule.mkQ _ a) = Submodule.mkQ _ (g a) :=
  rfl

public lemma adicQuotientMap_transition (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (h : I.map σ ≤ J)
    {m n : ℕ} (hmn : m ≤ n) (x : P ⧸ I ^ n • (⊤ : Submodule R P)) :
    AdicCompletion.transitionMap J Q hmn (adicQuotientMap g h n x) =
      adicQuotientMap g h m (AdicCompletion.transitionMap I P hmn x) := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective _ x
  rfl

/-- The map of adic completions induced by a semilinear map which carries the one adic ideal
into the other.  Mathlib's `AdicCompletion.map` is the case of a linear map and one ideal. -/
public noncomputable def adicCompletionMapₛₗ (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (h : I.map σ ≤ J) :
    AdicCompletion I P →ₛₗ[σ] AdicCompletion J Q where
  toFun x := ⟨fun n => adicQuotientMap g h n (x.val n), by
    intro m n hmn
    rw [adicQuotientMap_transition, x.property hmn]⟩
  map_add' x y := by ext n; exact map_add _ _ _
  map_smul' r x := by
    ext n
    exact (adicQuotientMap g h n).map_smulₛₗ r (x.val n)

public lemma adicCompletionMapₛₗ_of (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (h : I.map σ ≤ J) (x : P) :
    adicCompletionMapₛₗ g h (AdicCompletion.of I P x) = AdicCompletion.of J Q (g x) := by
  ext n
  rfl

public lemma adicCompletionMapₛₗ_continuous (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (h : I.map σ ≤ J) :
    SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I J (adicCompletionMapₛₗ g h) := by
  intro n
  refine ⟨n, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  change adicQuotientMap g h n (AdicCompletion.eval I P n x) = 0
  rw [hx, map_zero]

public lemma adicCompletionMapₛₗ_comp_apply {T V : Type*} [CommRing T] [AddCommGroup V]
    [Module T V] {τ : S →+* T} {ρ : R →+* T} {L : Ideal T}
    (g : P →ₛₗ[σ] Q) (k : Q →ₛₗ[τ] V) (l : P →ₛₗ[ρ] V)
    (hg : I.map σ ≤ J) (hk : J.map τ ≤ L) (hl : I.map ρ ≤ L)
    (hcomp : ∀ x, l x = k (g x)) (x : AdicCompletion I P) :
    adicCompletionMapₛₗ l hl x = adicCompletionMapₛₗ k hk (adicCompletionMapₛₗ g hg x) := by
  apply AdicCompletion.ext
  intro n
  change adicQuotientMap l hl n (x.val n) =
    adicQuotientMap k hk n (adicQuotientMap g hg n (x.val n))
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective _ (x.val n)
  rw [← ha, adicQuotientMap_mkQ, adicQuotientMap_mkQ, adicQuotientMap_mkQ, hcomp]

public lemma adicCompletionMapₛₗ_id_apply {ρ : R →+* R} (g : P →ₛₗ[ρ] P)
    (hg : I.map ρ ≤ I) (hid : ∀ x, g x = x) (x : AdicCompletion I P) :
    adicCompletionMapₛₗ g hg x = x := by
  apply AdicCompletion.ext
  intro n
  change adicQuotientMap g hg n (x.val n) = x.val n
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective _ (x.val n)
  rw [← ha, adicQuotientMap_mkQ, hid]

variable {P' Q' : Type*} [AddCommGroup P'] [Module R P'] [AddCommGroup Q'] [Module R Q']

/-- The map of adic completions induced by a linear map, as a linear map over the uncompleted
ring. -/
public noncomputable def adicCompletionMapLinear (g : P' →ₗ[R] Q') (I : Ideal R) :
    AdicCompletion I P' →ₗ[R] AdicCompletion I Q' :=
  adicCompletionMapₛₗ g (le_of_eq (Ideal.map_id I))

public lemma adicCompletionMapLinear_of (g : P' →ₗ[R] Q') (I : Ideal R) (x : P') :
    adicCompletionMapLinear g I (AdicCompletion.of I P' x) = AdicCompletion.of I Q' (g x) :=
  adicCompletionMapₛₗ_of g (le_of_eq (Ideal.map_id I)) x

public lemma adicCompletionMapLinear_continuous (g : P' →ₗ[R] Q') (I : Ideal R) :
    SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I I (adicCompletionMapLinear g I) :=
  adicCompletionMapₛₗ_continuous g (le_of_eq (Ideal.map_id I))

public lemma adicCompletionMapLinear_id (I : Ideal R) :
    adicCompletionMapLinear (LinearMap.id (R := R) (M := P')) I = LinearMap.id :=
  LinearMap.ext fun x => adicCompletionMapₛₗ_id_apply _ _ (fun _ => rfl) x

public lemma adicCompletionMapLinear_zero (I : Ideal R) :
    adicCompletionMapLinear (0 : P' →ₗ[R] Q') I = 0 := by
  apply LinearMap.ext
  intro x
  apply AdicCompletion.ext
  intro n
  change adicQuotientMap (0 : P' →ₗ[R] Q') _ n (x.val n) = 0
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective _ (x.val n)
  rw [← ha, adicQuotientMap_mkQ, LinearMap.zero_apply, map_zero]

/-- Two adically continuous additive maps between adic completions which agree on the canonical
image of the uncompleted module are equal, because every element of the completion is
approximated by that image to any prescribed order. -/
public lemma adicCompletion_addMonoidHom_ext {F G : AdicCompletion I P →+ AdicCompletion J Q}
    (hF : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I J F)
    (hG : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I J G)
    (h : ∀ x, F (AdicCompletion.of I P x) = G (AdicCompletion.of I P x)) : F = G := by
  apply AddMonoidHom.ext
  intro x
  apply AdicCompletion.ext
  intro n
  obtain ⟨mF, hmF⟩ := hF n
  obtain ⟨mG, hmG⟩ := hG n
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := Submodule.mkQ_surjective (I ^ max mF mG • (⊤ : Submodule R P))
    (AdicCompletion.eval I P (max mF mG) x)
  have hmax : AdicCompletion.eval I P (max mF mG) (x - AdicCompletion.of I P y) = 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, AdicCompletion.eval_of, hy, sub_self]
  have key : ∀ m, m ≤ max mF mG → AdicCompletion.eval I P m (x - AdicCompletion.of I P y) = 0 :=
    fun m hm => by simpa using congrArg (AdicCompletion.transitionMap I P hm) hmax
  have hF0 := hmF _ (key _ (Nat.le_max_left mF mG))
  have hG0 := hmG _ (key _ (Nat.le_max_right mF mG))
  simp only [map_sub] at hF0 hG0
  change AdicCompletion.eval J Q n (F x) = AdicCompletion.eval J Q n (G x)
  exact (sub_eq_zero.mp hF0).trans <| (congrArg (AdicCompletion.eval J Q n) (h y)).trans <|
    (sub_eq_zero.mp hG0).symm

/-- A map which factors through two adically continuous maps is adically continuous. -/
public lemma adicContinuous_of_comp {T V : Type*} [CommRing T] [AddCommGroup V] [Module T V]
    {L : Ideal T} {F : AdicCompletion I P → AdicCompletion J Q}
    {G : AdicCompletion J Q → AdicCompletion L V}
    {H : AdicCompletion I P → AdicCompletion L V}
    (hF : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I J F)
    (hG : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous J L G)
    (hH : ∀ x, H x = G (F x)) :
    SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous I L H := by
  intro n
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hG n
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := hF m
  refine ⟨l, fun x hx => ?_⟩
  rw [hH]
  exact hm _ (hl x hx)

end SemilinearCompletion

/-! ### Semilinear data as a presheaf of modules -/

section OfSemilinearData

variable {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}

/-- The transition map of a cosimplicial module along an identity is the identity. -/
public lemma cosimplicialModule_map_id_apply (M : CosimplicialModule A)
    (X : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ) (y : M.obj X) : M.map (𝟙 X) y = y := by
  rw [M.map_id, ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'_inv_app,
    ModuleCat.restrictScalarsId'App_inv_apply]

/-- A degree of a cosimplicial module presented by semilinear data is a module over the
corresponding degree of the presheaf of rings of the cosimplicial ring. -/
public instance moduleSemilinearCosimplicialModuleObj
    (M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, u} A) (X : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ) :
    Module (((unopUnop SimplexCategory ⋙ A) ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).obj X)
      (M.obj (unop (unop X))) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module (A.obj (unop (unop X))) (M.obj (unop (unop X))))

/-- A cosimplicial module presented by its degreewise modules and semilinear transition maps,
read as a presheaf of modules over the presheaf of rings of the cosimplicial ring.  This
compares the two presentations of a cosimplicial module used in Tag 07KQ, in the case where the
carriers live in the universe of the rings. -/
public noncomputable def SemilinearCosimplicialModule.toCosimplicialModule
    (M : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, u} A) : CosimplicialModule A where
  obj X := ModuleCat.of _ (M.obj (unop (unop X)))
  map {_ Y} φ := ModuleCat.ofHom
    (Y := (ModuleCat.restrictScalars
        (((unopUnop SimplexCategory ⋙ A) ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat RingCat).map φ).hom).obj
      (ModuleCat.of _ (M.obj (unop (unop Y)))))
    { toFun := M.map φ.unop.unop
      map_add' := map_add _
      map_smul' := fun r x => (M.map φ.unop.unop).map_smulₛₗ r x }
  map_id X := ModuleCat.hom_ext <| LinearMap.ext fun x => M.map_id_apply (unop (unop X)) x
  map_comp φ ψ := ModuleCat.hom_ext <| LinearMap.ext fun x =>
    M.map_comp_apply φ.unop.unop ψ.unop.unop x

end OfSemilinearData

/-! ### The degreewise adic completion of a cosimplicial module -/

section CosimplicialCompletion

variable {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}

/-- The degreewise adic completion of a cosimplicial module along a cosimplicial ideal, as
semilinear data: in degree `n` the adic completion of that degree of the module, with the
canonical semilinear extensions of the transition maps. -/
public noncomputable def CosimplicialIdeal.completionData (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    (M : CosimplicialModule A) : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.{u, u} A where
  obj n := AdicCompletion (I.obj n) (M.obj (op (op n)))
  addCommGroup _n := inferInstance
  module _n := inferInstance
  map φ := adicCompletionMapₛₗ (M.restrictₛₗ φ.op.op) (I.map_le φ)
  map_id_apply n x := adicCompletionMapₛₗ_id_apply _ _
    (fun y => cosimplicialModule_map_id_apply M (op (op n)) y) x
  map_comp_apply φ ψ x := adicCompletionMapₛₗ_comp_apply _ _ _ _ _ _
    (fun y => M.map_comp_apply φ.op.op ψ.op.op y) x

/-- The degreewise adic completion of a cosimplicial module along a cosimplicial ideal. -/
public noncomputable def CosimplicialIdeal.completion (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    (M : CosimplicialModule A) : CosimplicialModule A :=
  (I.completionData M).toCosimplicialModule

/-- The degreewise adic completion of a linear map in one cosimplicial degree. -/
public noncomputable def CosimplicialIdeal.completionLinearMap (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K M : CosimplicialModule A} (X : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ) (f : K.obj X ⟶ M.obj X) :
    (I.completion K).obj X ⟶ (I.completion M).obj X :=
  ModuleCat.ofHom (adicCompletionMapLinear f.hom (I.obj (unop (unop X))))

/-- Two linear maps which commute with a transition map of the cosimplicial modules have
completions which commute with the corresponding transition map of the completions: both sides
are adically continuous and agree on the canonical image of the uncompleted module. -/
public lemma completion_naturality (I : CosimplicialIdeal A) {K M : CosimplicialModule A}
    {X Y : (SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ)ᵒᵖ} (φ : X ⟶ Y)
    (f : K.obj X →ₗ[A.obj (unop (unop X))] M.obj X)
    (g : K.obj Y →ₗ[A.obj (unop (unop Y))] M.obj Y)
    (hnat : ∀ y : K.obj X, g (K.map φ y) = M.map φ (f y))
    (x : AdicCompletion (I.obj (unop (unop X))) (K.obj X)) :
    adicCompletionMapLinear g (I.obj (unop (unop Y)))
        (adicCompletionMapₛₗ (K.restrictₛₗ φ) (I.map_le φ.unop.unop) x) =
      adicCompletionMapₛₗ (M.restrictₛₗ φ) (I.map_le φ.unop.unop)
        (adicCompletionMapLinear f (I.obj (unop (unop X))) x) := by
  let F : AdicCompletion (I.obj (unop (unop X))) (K.obj X) →+
      AdicCompletion (I.obj (unop (unop Y))) (M.obj Y) :=
    (adicCompletionMapLinear g (I.obj (unop (unop Y)))).toAddMonoidHom.comp
      (adicCompletionMapₛₗ (K.restrictₛₗ φ) (I.map_le φ.unop.unop)).toAddMonoidHom
  let G : AdicCompletion (I.obj (unop (unop X))) (K.obj X) →+
      AdicCompletion (I.obj (unop (unop Y))) (M.obj Y) :=
    (adicCompletionMapₛₗ (M.restrictₛₗ φ) (I.map_le φ.unop.unop)).toAddMonoidHom.comp
      (adicCompletionMapLinear f (I.obj (unop (unop X)))).toAddMonoidHom
  have hF : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous (I.obj (unop (unop X)))
      (I.obj (unop (unop Y))) F :=
    adicContinuous_of_comp (adicCompletionMapₛₗ_continuous (K.restrictₛₗ φ) (I.map_le φ.unop.unop))
      (adicCompletionMapLinear_continuous g (I.obj (unop (unop Y)))) (fun _ => rfl)
  have hG : SemilinearCosimplicialModule.AdicContinuous (I.obj (unop (unop X)))
      (I.obj (unop (unop Y))) G :=
    adicContinuous_of_comp (adicCompletionMapLinear_continuous f (I.obj (unop (unop X))))
      (adicCompletionMapₛₗ_continuous (M.restrictₛₗ φ) (I.map_le φ.unop.unop)) (fun _ => rfl)
  have h : F = G := adicCompletion_addMonoidHom_ext hF hG (fun y => by
    change adicCompletionMapLinear g _
        (adicCompletionMapₛₗ (K.restrictₛₗ φ) _ (AdicCompletion.of _ _ y)) =
      adicCompletionMapₛₗ (M.restrictₛₗ φ) _
        (adicCompletionMapLinear f _ (AdicCompletion.of _ _ y))
    rw [adicCompletionMapₛₗ_of, adicCompletionMapLinear_of, adicCompletionMapLinear_of,
      adicCompletionMapₛₗ_of]
    exact congrArg (AdicCompletion.of (I.obj (unop (unop Y))) (M.obj Y)) (hnat y))
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun h x

/-- The degreewise adic completion of a homomorphism of cosimplicial modules. -/
public noncomputable def CosimplicialIdeal.completionHom (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K M : CosimplicialModule A} (φ : K ⟶ M) : I.completion K ⟶ I.completion M where
  app X := I.completionLinearMap X (φ.app X)
  naturality := fun {X Y} f => ModuleCat.hom_ext <| LinearMap.ext fun x =>
    completion_naturality I f (φ.app X).hom (φ.app Y).hom
      (fun y => PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply φ f y) x

public lemma CosimplicialIdeal.completionHom_id (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    (K : CosimplicialModule A) : I.completionHom (𝟙 K) = 𝟙 (I.completion K) := by
  apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
  intro X
  apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
  exact adicCompletionMapLinear_id (P' := K.obj X) (I.obj (unop (unop X)))

public lemma CosimplicialIdeal.completionHom_zero (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K M : CosimplicialModule A} : I.completionHom (0 : K ⟶ M) = 0 := by
  apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
  intro X
  apply ModuleCat.hom_ext
  exact adicCompletionMapLinear_zero (P' := K.obj X) (Q' := M.obj X) (I.obj (unop (unop X)))

/-- The degreewise adic completion of a homotopy of homomorphisms of cosimplicial modules: its
component at a simplex of `Δ[1]` is the completion of the original component. -/
public noncomputable def CosimplicialIdeal.completionHomotopy (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K M : CosimplicialModule A} {φ ψ : K ⟶ M} (h : Homotopy φ ψ) :
    Homotopy (I.completionHom φ) (I.completionHom ψ) where
  app n α := I.completionLinearMap (op (op n)) (h.app n α)
  naturality := fun {n m} f α => ModuleCat.hom_ext <| LinearMap.ext fun x =>
    completion_naturality I f.op.op (h.app n ((Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).map f.op α)).hom
      (h.app m α).hom (fun y => ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (h.naturality f α) y) x
  app_zero n := congrArg (I.completionLinearMap (op (op n))) (h.app_zero n)
  app_one n := congrArg (I.completionLinearMap (op (op n))) (h.app_one n)

/-- Homotopic homomorphisms of cosimplicial modules stay homotopic after degreewise adic
completion.  This is the completion part of Tag 07KQ for cosimplicial modules presented as
presheaves of modules; the tag itself sits on `Crystalline.homotopic_adicCompletionMap`, the
same statement for the presentation whose carriers live in an independent universe. -/
public theorem homotopic_completionHom (I : CosimplicialIdeal A) {K M : CosimplicialModule A}
    {φ ψ : K ⟶ M} (h : Homotopic φ ψ) :
    Homotopic (I.completionHom φ) (I.completionHom ψ) :=
  Relation.EqvGen.map (fun f => I.completionHom f)
    (fun _ _ ⟨hab⟩ => ⟨I.completionHomotopy hab⟩) h

/-- If the identity of a cosimplicial module is homotopic to zero, the same holds for its
degreewise adic completion. -/
public theorem homotopic_id_completion_zero (I : CosimplicialIdeal A)
    {K : CosimplicialModule A} (h : Homotopic (𝟙 K) 0) :
    Homotopic (𝟙 (I.completion K)) 0 := by
  have hc := homotopic_completionHom I h
  rwa [I.completionHom_id, I.completionHom_zero] at hc

/-- The ideals generated by `p` in the degrees of a cosimplicial ring form a cosimplicial
ideal, since every ring map carries `p` to `p`. -/
public def pAdicCosimplicialIdeal (A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}) (p : ℕ) :
    CosimplicialIdeal A where
  obj n := DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal (A := (A.obj n : Type u)) p
  map_le φ := by
    simp [DividedPowers.pAdicIdeal, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]

end CosimplicialCompletion

/-! ### Exterior powers and tensor products of a module homotopic to zero -/

section ExteriorAndTensor

variable {A : CosimplicialObject CommRingCat.{u}}

/-- A positive exterior power of the zero homomorphism of cosimplicial modules is zero: an
exterior product with a zero factor vanishes.  For `i = 0` this fails, the exterior power of
the zero map being the identity of the base ring. -/
public lemma exteriorPowerFunctor_map_zero {K M : CosimplicialModule A} {i : ℕ} (hi : 0 < i) :
    (exteriorPowerFunctor A i).functor.map (0 : K ⟶ M) = 0 := by
  apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
  intro X
  apply ModuleCat.exteriorPower.hom_ext
  apply ModuleCat.AlternatingMap.ext
  intro x
  change ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map (0 : K.obj X ⟶ M.obj X) i
      (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk x) = 0
  rw [ModuleCat.exteriorPower.map_mk]
  exact _root_.AlternatingMap.map_coord_zero
    (f := (ModuleCat.exteriorPower.mk :
      ModuleCat.AlternatingMap (M.obj X) ((M.obj X).exteriorPower i) i))
    ⟨0, hi⟩ (by simp)

/-- If the identity of a cosimplicial module is homotopic to zero, the same holds for every
positive exterior power. -/
public theorem homotopic_id_exteriorPower_zero {K : CosimplicialModule A} {i : ℕ} (hi : 0 < i)
    (h : Homotopic (𝟙 K) 0) :
    Homotopic (𝟙 ((exteriorPowerFunctor A i).functor.obj K)) 0 := by
  have hm := homotopic_exteriorPower_map i h
  rwa [exteriorPowerFunctor_map_zero hi, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id] at hm

/-- Tensoring homotopic homomorphisms of cosimplicial modules on the left with the identity of
another cosimplicial module preserves homotopy.  This is the left-handed companion of the
tensor part of Tag 07KQ, whose tag sits on the right-handed
`Crystalline.homotopic_tensor_id`. -/
public theorem homotopic_id_tensor {K M : CosimplicialModule A} {φ ψ : K ⟶ M}
    (h : Homotopic φ ψ) (L : CosimplicialModule A) :
    Homotopic (𝟙 L ⊗ₘ φ) (𝟙 L ⊗ₘ ψ) := by
  apply Relation.EqvGen.map (fun g => 𝟙 L ⊗ₘ g) (fun a b hab => ?_) h
  obtain ⟨hab⟩ := hab
  refine ⟨{ app := fun n α => 𝟙 (L.obj (op (op n))) ⊗ₘ hab.app n α,
            naturality := ?_, app_zero := ?_, app_one := ?_ }⟩
  · intro n m g α
    apply ModuleCat.MonoidalCategory.tensor_ext
    intro y z
    change L.map g.op.op y ⊗ₜ hab.app m α (K.map g.op.op z) =
      L.map g.op.op y ⊗ₜ M.map g.op.op (hab.app n ((Δ[1] : SSet.{0}).map g.op α) z)
    congr 1
    exact ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (hab.naturality g α) z
  · intro n
    rw [hab.app_zero]
    rfl
  · intro n
    rw [hab.app_one]
    rfl

/-- If the identity of a cosimplicial module is homotopic to zero, the same holds after
tensoring with any cosimplicial module. -/
public theorem homotopic_id_tensor_zero {K : CosimplicialModule A} (h : Homotopic (𝟙 K) 0)
    (L : CosimplicialModule A) : Homotopic (𝟙 (L ⊗ K)) 0 := by
  have hh := homotopic_id_tensor h L
  have hz : (𝟙 L ⊗ₘ (0 : K ⟶ K)) = 0 := by
    apply PresheafOfModules.hom_ext
    intro X
    apply ModuleCat.MonoidalCategory.tensor_ext
    intro y z
    change y ⊗ₜ (0 : K.obj X) = 0
    exact TensorProduct.tmul_zero _ _
  rw [MonoidalCategory.id_tensorHom_id] at hh
  simpa only [hz] using hh

end ExteriorAndTensor

/-! ### The vanishing of the completed forms -/

section Vanishing

variable {s : AffineCrystallineSituation.{u, v}} {ι : Type w}
  {f : MvPolynomial ι s.A →ₐ[s.A] s.C} {hf : Function.Surjective f}

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07LA.** With the notation of the equations (07JF) for `D(n)` and
(07L0) for `Ω_{D(n)}`, given any cosimplicial module `M_*` over `D(*)` and any `i > 0`, the
cosimplicial module

`M_0 ⊗̂_{D(0)} Ω^i_{D(0)} → M_1 ⊗̂_{D(1)} Ω^i_{D(1)} → M_2 ⊗̂_{D(2)} Ω^i_{D(2)} → ⋯`

is homotopic to zero, where `Ω^i_{D(n)}` is the `p`-adic completion of the `i`-th exterior power
of `Ω_{D(n)}` and `⊗̂` is the `p`-adic completion of the tensor product.

By Tag 07L9 the identity and the zero endomorphism of `Ω_{D(*)}` are homotopic.  Applying the
functor `∧^i` keeps them homotopic, and for `i > 0` turns the zero endomorphism into the zero
endomorphism, so the identity of `∧^i Ω_{D(*)}` is homotopic to zero; the `p`-adic completion
functor then gives the same for `Ω^i_{D(*)}`, tensoring with `M_*` gives it for
`M_* ⊗_{D(*)} Ω^i_{D(*)}`, and a final `p`-adic completion finishes the proof. -/
@[stacks 07LA]
public theorem id_completedTensorCompletedForms_homotopic_zero
    (E : CosimplicialEnvelope s f hf) (M : CosimplicialModule E.ring) {i : ℕ} (hi : 0 < i) :
    Homotopic (𝟙 ((pAdicCosimplicialIdeal E.ring s.p).completion
      (M ⊗ (pAdicCosimplicialIdeal E.ring s.p).completion
        ((exteriorPowerFunctor E.ring i).functor.obj E.differentials)))) 0 := by
  have hΩ : Homotopic (𝟙 E.differentials) 0 :=
    id_cosimplicialEnvelopeDifferentials_homotopic_zero E
  have hExterior := homotopic_id_exteriorPower_zero hi hΩ
  have hForms := homotopic_id_completion_zero (pAdicCosimplicialIdeal E.ring s.p) hExterior
  exact homotopic_id_completion_zero (pAdicCosimplicialIdeal E.ring s.p)
    (homotopic_id_tensor_zero hForms M)

end Vanishing

end Crystalline

end
